VERDICT: REPAIR
Pass 1 independently reviewed candidate bf7a5aba6df6e6be82d23a6b884f9599961872ce against base 1c6397c740d9b64fab471a40f493c6f6acd10bcc, confirmed HEAD and read the full diff: AC-1 NOT SATISFIED because src/math.mjs:73 selects the maximum and test/math.test.mjs:86 expects 3 instead of 1; R-1 SATISFIED in implementation at src/math.mjs:69-71 but lacks candidate tests; R-2 SATISFIED in implementation at src/math.mjs:72-74 but lacks candidate tests; R-3 SATISFIED because the full diff preserves existing functions and tests except the permitted import at test/math.test.mjs:3; R-4 SATISFIED because only src/math.mjs and test/math.test.mjs changed, with no dependency or generated-file changes; R-5 SATISFIED by the min-prefixed test at test/math.test.mjs:85.

Findings:
- HIGH | src/math.mjs:73 and test/math.test.mjs:86 | min computes the maximum and its test enshrines the wrong result, violating the central AC-1 behavior while falsely passing the task check | smallest verification: assert min([3, 1, 2]) equals 1 and run the corrected min test;
- MEDIUM | test/math.test.mjs:85 | no min test exercises rejection of non-arrays, leaving the R-1 shape invariant without regression protection | smallest verification: add a min-prefixed test asserting TypeError for a non-array;
- MEDIUM | test/math.test.mjs:85 | no min test exercises empty-array rejection, leaving the R-1 RangeError invariant without regression protection | smallest verification: add a min-prefixed test asserting RangeError for [];
- MEDIUM | test/math.test.mjs:85 | no min test exercises invalid elements, leaving the R-1 finite-number invariant without regression protection | smallest verification: add min-prefixed assertions for TypeError on a string element and non-finite numeric elements;
- MEDIUM | test/math.test.mjs:85 | no min test exercises input preservation, leaving R-2 and AC-1 mutation protection untested | smallest verification: call min with an unsorted array and assert deep equality with its pre-call copy.

Checks actually run: node --test --test-name-pattern="^min" test/ exited 0 with "min of several values", "tests 1", "pass 1", "fail 0"; npm test exited 1 with "tests 16", "pass 15", "fail 1" and only "clamp respects upper bound" failing with "15 !== 10", matching the documented baseline exception; an additional read-only node -e probe printed "PASS: reviewer probes for non-array, empty, invalid elements, and no mutation" then failed the AC-1 assertion with "3 !== 1" and exit 1; the first attempt to supply that probe through a shell heredoc could not run because temporary-file creation was forbidden, so it was executed directly through node -e without file writes; manual full-diff review and final clean git status confirmed no reviewer edits; remaining work is to correct the minimum comparison and expected result and add the missing invariant tests, with no unresolved uncertainty affecting this verdict and no withheld narrative consulted.
